### REST Client Test File for VS Code (REST Client Extension)
@authHost = http://localhost:4000
@blogHost = http://localhost:5000

### -------------------------------------------------------------
### AUTH SERVER ENDPOINTS (:4000)
### -------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "examuser",
  "email": "examuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login as newly registered user (captures JWT token automatically)
# @name login
POST {{authHost}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "examuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Save auth token from login response
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 4. Verify Current User Token (/me)
GET {{authHost}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### -------------------------------------------------------------
### BLOG SERVER ENDPOINTS (:5000)
### -------------------------------------------------------------

### 5. Get all blog posts (Public)
GET {{blogHost}}/api/posts

### 6. Get single blog post by ID (Public)
GET {{blogHost}}/api/posts/1

### 7. Create a new blog post (Authenticated)
# @name createPost
POST {{blogHost}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Post Created from REST Client",
  "content": "This post tests authenticated creation in the blog server."
}

### 8. Update blog post by ID (Author or Admin only)
PUT {{blogHost}}/api/posts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Post Title",
  "content": "Content updated via REST Client test."
}

### 9. Delete blog post by ID (Author or Admin only)
DELETE {{blogHost}}/api/posts/2
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
